      "summary": "The DDX class is a planned Italian Navy guided-missile destroyer, with two ships ordered from Orizzonte Sistemi Navali in 2026, designed for integrated air and missile defence to replace the Durand de la Penne class. Key figures: displacement 13,500 tons, length 180 m, crew 251. Not yet in service; on order for 1 navy — Italy.",
