      "summary": "The Etna-class is an Italian-designed replenishment oiler with two ships built: the Italian Navy's Etna, commissioned in 1998, and the Hellenic Navy's HS Prometheus, delivered in 2003, both performing underway replenishment. Key figures: displacement 13,400 tons, length 147 m, top speed 21 knots, crew 240, built 2. In service with 2 navies — Greece (1), Italy (1).",
