      "summary": "The Henry J. Kaiser class is a series of US Navy fleet replenishment oilers operated by Military Sealift Command since 1986, with a mostly civilian crew, one of which now serves the Chilean Navy. Key figures: displacement 41,353 tons, length 206 m, top speed 20 knots, crew 89, built 16. In service with 2 navies — United States (11), Chile (1).",
