      "summary": "Ordered in 2013, Singapore's Invincible-class is a German-built diesel-electric attack submarine distinguished by a design derived from the Type 214 export submarine. Key figures: displacement 2,000 tons, length 70 m, top speed 10 knots, crew 28, unit cost $680M, built 6. In service with 1 navy — Singapore (2).",
