      "summary": "Commissioned by France in 2023, the Jacques Chevallier-class auxiliary ship provides fleet replenishment and features a double-hull design based on the Italian Vulcano class. Key figures: displacement 31,000 tons, length 194 m, top speed 20 knots, crew 130, built 2. In service with 1 navy — France (2).",
