      "summary": "The John Lewis class is a series of US Navy fleet replenishment oilers built by NASSCO and operated by Military Sealift Command, in service since 2022, with a double hull built to commercial tanker standards. Key figures: displacement 49,850 tons, length 227 m, top speed 20 knots, crew 125, built 6. In service with 1 navy — United States (6).",
