      "summary": "The Lewis and Clark class is a series of 14 US Navy dry cargo and ammunition ships operated by Military Sealift Command since 2006 to resupply naval forces at sea, with only light defensive armament. Key figures: displacement 45,149 tons, length 210 m, top speed 21 knots, crew 135, built 14. In service with 1 navy — United States (14).",
