      "summary": "Commissioned by Japan in 2004, the Mashū-class replenishment oiler provides underway logistics support and features an enclosed helicopter hangar for vertical replenishment operations. Key figures: displacement 13,500 tons, length 221 m, top speed 24 knots, crew 150, built 2. In service with 1 navy — Japan (2).",
