      "summary": "Ordered by the Royal Canadian Navy and built by Seaspan, the Protecteur-class joint support ship adapts the German Berlin design for replenishment, sealift and medical support. Key figures: displacement 20,240 tons, length 174 m, top speed 20 knots, crew 199, unit cost $4.1B, built 1. Not yet in service; on order for 1 navy — Canada.",
