      "description": "The Soyang-class (AOE-II) is a class of fast combat support ships built for the Republic of Korea Navy. Designed as the successor to the Cheonji-class, the vessels are constructed by Hyundai Heavy Industries and Hanwha Ocean. The lead ship of the class, ROKS Soyang , was laid down on 13 July 2015, launched on 29 November 2016, and commissioned on 18 September 2018. A contract for a second vessel of the class was announced on 26 July 2024, with its commissioning scheduled for December 2028.\n\nThe vessels utilize a combined diesel-electric or diesel propulsion system that integrates hybrid diesel and electric engines driving propulsion shafts. Design features include an embarked helicopter facility featuring a helipad and hangar, capable of supporting aircraft such as the SH-60 Seahawk . For self-defense, the ships are equipped with a close-in weapon system and decoy launchers.\n\nThe lead vessel, ROKS Soyang , remains in active service.",
