      "summary": "Commissioned by the Royal Australian Navy in 2021, the Supply-class replenishment oiler is a Navantia design derived from the Spanish Cantabria, carrying fuel, dry stores and ammunition. Key figures: displacement 19,500 tons, length 174 m, top speed 20 knots, crew 122, built 2. In service with 1 navy — Australia (2).",
