      "summary": "Commissioned by the Soviet Union in 1985, the Vishnya-class auxiliary ship is an intelligence-gathering vessel distinguished by its prominent spherical radomes. Key figures: displacement 3,470 tons, length 92 m, top speed 16 knots, crew 146, built 7. In service with 1 navy — Russia (7).",
